  "configuration_id": "config_045",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_006: image_only, singleprofile, resnet50 → acc 0.208, F1 0.172), which is barely above chance, giving us very sparse evidence. The most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality has meaningful signal at all or whether ResNet50 is simply too weak a representation. Config_045 (image_only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l) is a clean single-variable comparison to config_006—only the image encoder changes—so it isolates the effect of representation quality. If ViT-L substantially improves accuracy, it tells us representation is a bottleneck and motivates investing in stronger encoders and multimodal fusion. If it does not, it strongly suggests the image modality has limited discriminative signal, redirecting the search toward RNA-only or multimodal configurations. This is the highest-information-per-experiment choice under the limited budget because it directly addresses the viability of the image modality before committing to more complex multimodal designs."
}

